ved","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:7497355ce6f4deec500ea969a68986d82777ebbc85787cd52eeff0e5ea67f3a5","file":"preprints/Directional-transience-implies-ballisticity-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex","line":50,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"22b9f6c2e876de8277bb8d4a39792b1f255a059ff06fbebd39f1c14531d405e2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Directional-transience-implies-ballisticity-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7497355ce6f4deec500ea969a68986d82777ebbc85787cd52eeff0e5ea67f3a5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Directional-transience-implies-ballisticity-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex#L50"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $d\\ge2$ and let $P=\\nu^{\\otimes\\mathbb Z^d}$ be an iid law of\nnearest-neighbor transition rows satisfying uniform ellipticity. If\n$\\ell\\in S^{d-1}$ and $P_0(A_\\ell)=1$, then there exists a deterministic\nvector $v=v(\\nu)\\in\\mathbb R^d$ such that\n\\[\n v\\cdot\\ell>0,\n \\qquad\n P_0\\!\\left(\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{X_n}{n}=v\\right)=1.\n\\]\nIn particular, the walk is ballistic in the same direction $\\ell$."}
